  "protocolVersion": 1,
  "name": "A re-stated band-assisted set keeps its sign and value",
  "description": "The phone holds a session whose first bench set is band-assisted at -20 kg and answers a snapshot request. The wrist logs its own assisted set at -22.5 kg under its own id, then the phone answers again with the entries it now holds: the assist it already carried, the wrist's own assisted set, and a new far-assist set at the floor of -200 kg. Because both stacks merge entries by entryId and re-state a held id rather than storing a second row, the assist neither duplicates nor becomes zero or positive: the phone converges on one row per id with the values the phone holds, and the wrist shows the same three ids with the load each one carries.",
